<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When the linear transformer is trained under gradient descent. Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)</annotation></semantics></math> have the following form:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(t)=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,,\quad\quad W(t)=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;cI&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;W_{24}(t)\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(t)=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,,\quad\quad W(t)=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;cI&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;W_{24}(t)\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{31}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{31}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{24}(t)\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{24}(t)\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> is very similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Lemma C.2]</cite>. The difference is that here the features covariance is non-identity, while we do not do CoT during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given that several blocks of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)</annotation></semantics></math> remain zero across the gradient updates, we can reduce the loss function in a simpler form. Define the shorthand <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}(t):=V_{31}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}(t):=V_{31}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t):=W_{24}(t)\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t):=W_{24}(t)\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Invoking (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In A.1.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) we can rewrite the loss as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left(\left\|\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
\hat{w}_{0}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
1\end{bmatrix}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left(\left\|\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
\hat{w}_{0}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
1\end{bmatrix}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(\tilde{V}(t)w(t)\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(\tilde{V}(t)w(t)\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Lambda}:=XX^{\top}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Lambda}:=XX^{\top}/n</annotation></semantics></math>. As we see <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)</annotation></semantics></math> does not provide additional degree of freedom in minimizing the loss since it appears as the term <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}(t)w(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}(t)w(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. This clarifies fixing <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)=-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)=-c</annotation></semantics></math> along the gradient updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{{\operatorname{tr}}}(c^{2}\tilde{V}\hat{\Lambda}^{2}\tilde{V}^{\top}+I+2c\tilde{V}\hat{\Lambda})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{{\operatorname{tr}}}(c^{2}\tilde{V}\hat{\Lambda}^{2}\tilde{V}^{\top}+I+2c\tilde{V}\hat{\Lambda})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with columns drawn i.i.d from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any deterministic matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}A\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\right)=\frac{n-1}{n}\Lambda A\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}\left(\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda A)\Lambda\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}A\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\right)=\frac{n-1}{n}\Lambda A\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}\left(\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda A)\Lambda\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}^{2})=\frac{n+1}{n}\Lambda^{2}+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda:=\Gamma\Lambda\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}^{2})=\frac{n+1}{n}\Lambda^{2}+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda:=\Gamma\Lambda\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}\left(\tilde{V}\Gamma\Lambda\tilde{V}^{\top}\right)+\frac{d}{2}+c\;{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\tilde{V}\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}\left(\tilde{V}\Gamma\Lambda\tilde{V}^{\top}\right)+\frac{d}{2}+c\;{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\tilde{V}\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">This is convex in <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and so gradient descent with a fixed step size <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq 1/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq 1/L</annotation></semantics></math> converges to its minimizer, if <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{V}L\preceq LI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{V}L\preceq LI</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\tilde{V}}^{2}L=c^{2}\Gamma\Lambda\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\tilde{V}}^{2}L=c^{2}\Gamma\Lambda\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">so we can take
<math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=c^{2}\left\|\Gamma\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=c^{2}\left\|\Gamma\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op}</annotation></semantics></math>. To find the minimizer of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we set its gradient to zero,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{c^{2}}{2}(\Gamma\Lambda\tilde{V}^{\top}+\tilde{V}\Gamma\Lambda)+c\Lambda=0\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{c^{2}}{2}(\Gamma\Lambda\tilde{V}^{\top}+\tilde{V}\Gamma\Lambda)+c\Lambda=0\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">which is a continuous-time Lyapunov equation (Note that <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> commute and both are symmetric). Hence, it has a unique solution given by <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}=-\frac{\Gamma^{-1}}{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}=-\frac{\Gamma^{-1}}{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As the final step, we show that <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are also a global optimum for the population loss, even without making the specific structure imposed by gradient descent as described in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We continue by computing the output of LSA, and recall that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{w}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{w}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;0\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}E_{\tau}^{\top}W\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
0\\
1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>X</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;0\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}E_{\tau}^{\top}W\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
0\\
1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d\times 1}&amp;0_{d\times 1}&amp;0_{d\times 1}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0_{1\times n}&amp;0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}W_{14}\\
W_{24}\\
W_{34}\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>34</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d\times 1}&amp;0_{d\times 1}&amp;0_{d\times 1}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0_{1\times n}&amp;0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}W_{14}\\
W_{24}\\
W_{34}\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+Xy^{\top}W_{24}\\
yX^{\top}W_{14}+yy^{\top}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}(t)\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+Xy^{\top}W_{24}\\
yX^{\top}W_{14}+yy^{\top}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}(t)\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\rm LSA}(E_{\tau},\theta)[:,-1]-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\rm LSA}(E_{\tau},\theta)[:,-1]-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
0\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+Xy^{\top}W_{24}\\
yX^{\top}W_{14}+yy^{\top}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
0\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+Xy^{\top}W_{24}\\
yX^{\top}W_{14}+yy^{\top}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+XX^{\top}w_{\tau}W_{24}\\
w_{\tau}^{\top}XX^{\top}W_{14}+w_{\tau}^{\top}XX^{\top}w_{\tau}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}W_{14}+XX^{\top}w_{\tau}W_{24}\\
w_{\tau}^{\top}XX^{\top}W_{14}+w_{\tau}^{\top}XX^{\top}w_{\tau}W_{24}\\
0\\
W_{44}\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
w_{\tau}\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">The loss function is the expected squared norm of this object. To minimize it, we can make its first, second and last entries zero by setting the corresponding rows in <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> to zero. This gives us</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|\frac{1}{n}(V_{31}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top})XX^{\top}(W_{14}+W_{24}w_{\tau})-w_{\tau}+\frac{1}{n}V_{34}W_{44}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>34</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|\frac{1}{n}(V_{31}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top})XX^{\top}(W_{14}+W_{24}w_{\tau})-w_{\tau}+\frac{1}{n}V_{34}W_{44}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}+\frac{1}{n}V_{34}W_{44}+(V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}-I)w_{\tau}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>34</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>44</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}+\frac{1}{n}V_{34}W_{44}+(V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}-I)w_{\tau}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}-I)w_{\tau}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}\hat{\Lambda}W_{24}-I)w_{\tau}+V_{32}w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}W_{24}\hat{\Lambda}+V_{32}W_{14}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}W_{24}\hat{\Lambda}+V_{32}W_{14}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">where the penultimate step holds since the cross term is an odd function of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and so its expectation is zero. The other eliminated term is squared and so non-negative. In the last step we used that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}^{\top}\hat{\Lambda}W_{14}</annotation></semantics></math> is scalar and so can be replaced by its transpose. In addition <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{24}</annotation></semantics></math> is also scalar and can commute with <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. now observe that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{32}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>14</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{14}</annotation></semantics></math> do not offer any flexibility in minimizing the loss function as their effect can be absorbed in <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{31}W_{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{31}W_{24}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can set them to zero. Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{V,W}L(\theta)\geq\min_{V_{31},W_{24}}\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}W_{24}\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{V,W}L(\theta)\geq\min_{V_{31},W_{24}}\frac{1}{2}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|(V_{31}W_{24}\hat{\Lambda}-I)w_{\tau}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p">Observe that the right-hand side is of the form (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) and hence its global optimum (reached by gradient descent) serves as the global minimum of the loss.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove this lemma, we prove that when the irrelevant blocks are 0, the gradients of the loss remain zero on those blocks and they never update the corresponding parameter block.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We do induction on <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that the claim holds for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by computing the output of LSA.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}E_{\tau}^{\top}W\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
\hat{w}_{0}\\
1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>X</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}E_{\tau}^{\top}W\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\\
\hat{w}_{0}\\
1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)X&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}c\hat{w}_{0}\\
W_{24}(t)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>X</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)X&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}X&amp;0\\
y&amp;0\\
0_{d\times n}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}c\hat{w}_{0}\\
W_{24}(t)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)X&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cX^{\top}\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)y^{\top}\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d\times n}&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\\
V_{31}(t)X&amp;0_{d}\\
0_{1\times n}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cX^{\top}\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)y^{\top}\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we used that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\top}=X^{\top}w_{\tau}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\top}=X^{\top}w_{\tau}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. We proceed with calculating the derivatives of the loss:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{V}L(\theta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>V</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{V}L(\theta(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\nabla_{V}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\nabla_{V}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We note that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">In addition,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}W^{\top}\frac{E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}c\hat{w}_{0}&amp;W_{24}(t)&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\begin{bmatrix}c\hat{w}_{0}&amp;W_{24}(t)&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}[c\hat{w}_{0}XX^{\top}+W_{24}(t)yX^{\top}\;\;c\hat{w}_{0}Xy^{\top}+W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\;\;0\;\;\;0]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>  0   0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}[c\hat{w}_{0}XX^{\top}+W_{24}(t)yX^{\top}\;\;c\hat{w}_{0}Xy^{\top}+W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\;\;0\;\;\;0]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Plugging in from (<a href="#A1.E5" title="In A.1.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E6" title="In A.1.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>) into (<a href="#A1.E4" title="In A.1.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>) we get the following structure for the gradient of the loss:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla L(\theta(t))=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\nabla_{V_{31}}L(\theta(t))&amp;\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla L(\theta(t))=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
\nabla_{V_{31}}L(\theta(t))&amp;\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\!\!\nabla_{V_{31}}L(\theta(t))\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\!\!\nabla_{V_{31}}L(\theta(t))\!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\!\frac{1}{n^{2}}\!\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}\!(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\!\left(c\hat{w}_{0}XX^{\top}\!\!+\!W_{24}(t)yX^{\top}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\!\frac{1}{n^{2}}\!\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}\!(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\!\left(c\hat{w}_{0}XX^{\top}\!\!+\!W_{24}(t)yX^{\top}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))\!</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\!\frac{1}{n^{2}}\!\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\!\left[\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\left(c\hat{w}_{0}Xy^{\top}\!\!+\!W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\!\frac{1}{n^{2}}\!\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\!\left[\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\left(c\hat{w}_{0}Xy^{\top}\!\!+\!W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Recall that we set <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{w}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{w}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by which we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{V_{32}}L(\theta(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left((V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\sf T}-nI)w_{\tau}W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left((V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\sf T}-nI)w_{\tau}W_{24}(t)yy^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{W_{24}(t)}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left((V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\sf T}-nI)w_{\tau}{w_{\tau}}^{\top}XX^{\top}w_{\tau}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{W_{24}(t)}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left((V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\sf T}-nI)w_{\tau}{w_{\tau}}^{\top}XX^{\top}w_{\tau}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">since it is an odd function of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. (Note that the population loss is non-random, due to the expectation in its definition. Since the initial <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(0),W(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(0),W(0)</annotation></semantics></math> are non-random, the trajectory <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are non-random.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next proceed with calculating the gradient with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{W}L(\theta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{W}L(\theta(t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\nabla_{W}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\nabla_{W}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\left\|f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}V^{\top}\left(f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}V^{\top}\left(f_{\mathrm{LSA}}(E_{\tau};\theta(t))_{[:,-1]}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau},1)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}V^{\top}\left(VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left[E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}V^{\top}\left(VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)\right)E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\\
yX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\\
yX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\right)\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the last step follows from the following equation and simple algebraic calculation:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}=\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\quad E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{\tau}E_{\tau}^{\top}=\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;\hat{w}_{0}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}^{\top}&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\quad E_{\tau}[:,-1]^{\top}=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;\hat{w}_{0}&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}\!\!(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\!\!+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.271em;" width="0.271em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle VE_{\tau}\cdot\frac{E_{\tau}^{\top}WE_{\tau}[:,-1]}{n}-(0_{d},0,w_{\tau}-\hat{w}_{0},0)=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
V_{31}(t)XX^{\top}\!\!(c\hat{w}_{0}+W_{24}(t)w_{\tau})\!\!+n(\hat{w}_{0}-w_{\tau})\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Recalling that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{w}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{w}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> we simplify <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W}L</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{W}L(\theta(t))=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}-nI)w_{\tau}\\
yX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}-nI\right)w_{\tau}\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>W</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{W}L(\theta(t))=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}-nI)w_{\tau}\\
yX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}\left(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}-nI\right)w_{\tau}\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}+nI)w_{\tau}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[XX^{\top}V_{31}(t)^{\top}(V_{31}(t)W_{24}(t)XX^{\top}+nI)w_{\tau}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{31}(t),W_{24}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{31}(t),W_{24}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are non-random and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero mean and independent of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{24}}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{24}}L</annotation></semantics></math> is the only non-zero block.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{E}\left[x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}Ax_{j}x_{j}^{\top}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{E}\left[x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}Ax_{j}x_{j}^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">There are <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n(n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math> terms where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> terms with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=j</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d., let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> denote either of them. Thus,</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n(n-1)\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]A\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]+n\,\mathbb{E}\left[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}\right]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\left(n(n-1)\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]A\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]+n\,\mathbb{E}\left[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The first term is the second moments. For the second term we use Isserlis’s theorem, by which we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}\left[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}\right]\right)_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}\left[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}\right]\right)_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k,l}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{k}A_{kl}x_{l}x_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k,l}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{k}A_{kl}x_{l}x_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k,l}A_{kl}\left(\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{k}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{l}x_{j}]+\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{l}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{k}x_{j}]+\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{j}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{l}x_{k}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k,l}A_{kl}\left(\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{k}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{l}x_{j}]+\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{l}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{k}x_{j}]+\mathbb{E}[x_{i}x_{j}]\,\mathbb{E}[x_{l}x_{k}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]=\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}]=\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}]=\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+\Lambda\,\operatorname{Tr}(A\Lambda)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[xx^{\top}Axx^{\top}]=\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+\Lambda\,\operatorname{Tr}(A\Lambda)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{n-1}{n^{2}}\Lambda A\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}\left(\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+\Lambda\,{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A\Lambda)\right)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[XX^{\top}AXX^{\top}\right]=\frac{n-1}{n^{2}}\Lambda A\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}\left(\Lambda(A+A^{\top})\Lambda+\Lambda\,{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A\Lambda)\right)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 ‣ 3.2 Test time chain-of-thought ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> given by (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Theorem 3.1 ‣ 3.1 In-Context Weight Prediction and Linear Self-attention ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>), as the estimated blocks of the transformer after training. We next rewrite the updates for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a more explicit form:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\rm LSA}(E_{i},\theta^{*})_{[:,-1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>LSA</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\rm LSA}(E_{i},\theta^{*})_{[:,-1]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+VE_{i}\cdot\frac{E_{i}^{\top}W{E_{i}}_{[:,-1]}}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+VE_{i}\cdot\frac{E_{i}^{\top}W{E_{i}}_{[:,-1]}}{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}VE_{i}E_{i}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}VE_{i}E_{i}^{\top}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}\\
0_{d\times d}&amp;0_{m\times m}\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}V\begin{bmatrix}XX^{\top}&amp;Xy^{\top}\\
yX^{\top}&amp;yy^{\top}\\
0_{d\times d}&amp;0_{m\times m}\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\\
V_{31}XX^{\top}&amp;V_{31}Xy^{\top}\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0_{d}\\
0\\
w_{i}\\
1\end{bmatrix}+\frac{1}{m}\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\\
V_{31}XX^{\top}&amp;V_{31}Xy^{\top}\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}cw_{i}\\
-c\\
0\\
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recalling that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{31}=\Gamma^{-1}/c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{31}=\Gamma^{-1}/c</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}y_{\rm test}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}y_{\rm test}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}(w_{i}-w_{\rm test})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{i}-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}(w_{i}-w_{\rm test})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rearranging the terms, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i+1}-w_{\rm test}=(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})(w_{i}-w_{\rm test})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i+1}-w_{\rm test}=(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})(w_{i}-w_{\rm test})</annotation></semantics></math> which results in</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}+(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})^{k}(w_{0}-w_{\rm test})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}+(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})^{k}(w_{0}-w_{\rm test})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(I-(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})^{k})w_{\rm test}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(I-(I-\frac{1}{m}\Gamma^{-1}X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top})^{k})w_{\rm test}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the shorthand <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Lambda}=X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Lambda}=X_{\rm test}X_{\rm test}^{\top}/m</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}((I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}))w_{\rm test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}((I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}))w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda-\Lambda\Gamma^{-1}+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-2}\hat{\Lambda}))w_{\rm test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda-\Lambda\Gamma^{-1}+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-2}\hat{\Lambda}))w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-2}\hat{\Lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-2}\hat{\Lambda})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{m-1}{m}\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+\frac{1}{m}(2\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{m-1}{m}\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+\frac{1}{m}(2\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{m+1}{m}\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+\frac{1}{m}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{m+1}{m}\Lambda\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda+\frac{1}{m}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> commute and both are symmetric we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-2\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda+\frac{m+1}{m}\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+\frac{1}{m}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)w_{\rm test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-2\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda+\frac{m+1}{m}\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+\frac{1}{m}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2}w_{\rm test}+\frac{1}{m}w_{\rm test}^{\top}(\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)w_{\rm test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=w_{\rm test}^{\top}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2}w_{\rm test}+\frac{1}{m}w_{\rm test}^{\top}(\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda)w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using the definition <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=(1+\frac{1}{n})\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=(1+\frac{1}{n})\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to see that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda\preceq\frac{1}{n}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda^{-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda\preceq\frac{1}{n}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Also since <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}\preceq\Lambda^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}\preceq\Lambda^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda\preceq I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})\Lambda" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-2}\Lambda^{2}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda\Gamma^{-2})\Lambda\preceq I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Combining the last two equations, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}_{X_{\rm test}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})\leq w_{\rm test}^{\top}\left(\frac{1}{n^{2}}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda^{-1})^{2}+\frac{1}{m}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})\Lambda)\right)w_{\rm test}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}_{X_{\rm test}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})\leq w_{\rm test}^{\top}\left(\frac{1}{n^{2}}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)\Lambda^{-1})^{2}+\frac{1}{m}(I+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})\Lambda)\right)w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Taking another expectation with respect to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\rm test}\sim{\sf N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\rm test}\sim{\sf N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> we get</p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})\leq\frac{1}{n^{2}}(d+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)^{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-2})+2{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})))+\frac{1}{m}(d+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|\hat{w}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})\leq\frac{1}{n^{2}}(d+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)^{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-2})+2{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})))+\frac{1}{m}(d+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The claim follows by noting</p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq d\frac{{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{\lambda_{\min}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq d\frac{{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{\lambda_{\min}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)^{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)^{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq d\Big(\frac{{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{\lambda_{\min}}\Big)^{2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq d\Big(\frac{{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{\lambda_{\min}}\Big)^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum eigenvalue of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Lambda}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{k}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Lambda}:=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{k}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. After <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> steps generation, we have <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k+1}=(I-(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k})w_{\rm test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k+1}=(I-(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k})w_{\rm test}</annotation></semantics></math> and so</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|w_{k+1}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k}w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k})\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|w_{k+1}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k}w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda})^{k})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> commute and both are symmetric. Therefore <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is also symmetric. We denote by <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
The matrix <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> however is not symmetric. We denote by <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Gamma^{-1}\hat{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Weyl’s inequality, we have <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\sigma_{i}-\hat{\sigma}_{i}|\leq\left\|\Gamma^{-1}(\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda})\right\|_{\rm op}:=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\sigma_{i}-\hat{\sigma}_{i}|\leq\left\|\Gamma^{-1}(\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda})\right\|_{\rm op}:=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\sigma_{i}}^{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\sigma_{i}}^{2k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(\sigma_{i}+\delta)^{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(\sigma_{i}+\delta)^{2k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{2k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\sum_{j=1}^{2k}{2k\choose j}\left(\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\sum_{j=1}^{2k}{2k\choose j}\left(\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\sum_{j=1}^{2k}(2k)^{j}\left(\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sigma_{i}^{2k}\left(1+\sum_{j=1}^{2k}(2k)^{j}\left(\frac{\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\right)^{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}_{i}:=\sum_{j=1}^{2k}(\frac{2k\delta}{\sigma_{i}})^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}_{i}:=\sum_{j=1}^{2k}(\frac{2k\delta}{\sigma_{i}})^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. We next proceed by bounding <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Lambda}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i\in[m]}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Lambda}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i\in[m]}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\sim{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\sim{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using concentration bounds on random matrices with independent sub-gaussian rows (See e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, Eq. 5.26]</cite>), we get that with probability at least <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2e^{-ct^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2e^{-ct^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda}\right\|_{\rm op}\leq\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2})\left\|\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op},\quad\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda}\right\|_{\rm op}\leq\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2})\left\|\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op},\quad\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> have bounded eigenvalues, by adjusting the constants <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C</annotation></semantics></math> (absorbing <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\Lambda\right\|_{\rm op}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\Gamma^{-1}\right\|_{\rm op}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\Gamma^{-1}\right\|_{\rm op}</annotation></semantics></math> into these constants), we also have that with probability at least <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2e^{-ct^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2e^{-ct^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta:=\left\|\Gamma^{-1}(\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda})\right\|_{\rm op}\leq\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2}),\quad\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta:=\left\|\Gamma^{-1}(\Lambda-\hat{\Lambda})\right\|_{\rm op}\leq\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2}),\quad\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define the probabilistic event <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}:=\{\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\leq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}:=\{\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\leq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Obviously, <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}})\leq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}})\leq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also have
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})=\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s){\rm d}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})=\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s){\rm d}s</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that by definition of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}_{i}=\sum_{j=1}^{2k}\Big(\frac{2k\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\Big)^{j}\leq 2k\max\Big(2k\delta/\sigma_{i},(2k\delta/\sigma_{i})^{2k}\Big)\leq C^{\prime}k\max(k\delta,(k\delta)^{2k})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}_{i}=\sum_{j=1}^{2k}\Big(\frac{2k\delta}{\sigma_{i}}\Big)^{j}\leq 2k\max\Big(2k\delta/\sigma_{i},(2k\delta/\sigma_{i})^{2k}\Big)\leq C^{\prime}k\max(k\delta,(k\delta)^{2k})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that since eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> are upper and lower bounded by constants, so are <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s. Therefore, we can work with one constant <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that works for all <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By virtue of the above bound, if <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq\min(\frac{s}{k^{2}},(\frac{s}{k^{2k+1}})^{\frac{1}{2k}})\geq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq\min(\frac{s}{k^{2}},(\frac{s}{k^{2k+1}})^{\frac{1}{2k}})\geq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})</annotation></semantics></math>. We next choose <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> such that for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=C\sqrt{\frac{d}{m}}+\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2})\leq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{2})\leq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, so that we can apply the tail bound (<a href="#A1.E12" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, for <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})\geq C\sqrt{d/m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})\geq C\sqrt{d/m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so it suffices to have <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}},\frac{t^{2}}{m})\leq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(\frac{t}{\sqrt{m}},\frac{t^{2}}{m})\leq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, we can set <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\min(\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k^{2}}s,\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k^{2}}s^{\frac{1}{2k}},\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k}\sqrt{s},\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k}s^{\frac{1}{4k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\min(\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k^{2}}s,\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k^{2}}s^{\frac{1}{2k}},\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k}\sqrt{s},\frac{\sqrt{m}}{k}s^{\frac{1}{4k}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s){\rm d}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\geq s){\rm d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\left(\delta\geq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\left(\delta\geq\frac{1}{k^{2}}\min(s,s^{\frac{1}{2k}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}2\exp(-ct^{2}){\rm d}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{Ck^{2}\sqrt{d/m}}^{\infty}2\exp(-ct^{2}){\rm d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">By considering each of the four terms in the minimum operator defining <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and following algebraic manipulation, it can be seen that the right-hand side above is <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k^{2}\sqrt{d/m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k^{2}\sqrt{d/m})</annotation></semantics></math> and hence,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}})+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})\leq C(k\sqrt{d/m})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}})+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{E}^{c}})\leq C(k\sqrt{d/m})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">for a constant <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining (<a href="#A1.E10" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.7 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>) and the bound <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Delta}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Delta}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|w_{k+1}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\left\|w_{k+1}-w_{\rm test}\right\|_{\ell_{2}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|(I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[\left\|(I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}\right\|_{F}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(a)}}{{\leq}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(a)}}{{\leq}}\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\sum_{i=1}^{d}\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(b)}}{{\leq}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(b)}}{{\leq}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(c)}}{{\leq}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+Ck\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(c)}}{{\leq}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+Ck\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{m}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2k})(1+Ck\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{m}})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2k})(1+Ck\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{m}})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>). In addition, step <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from the following lemma from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Eq.(3.3.39)]</cite>)
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a given <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> be a given positive integer. For all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{q}\sigma_{i}(A^{m})^{p}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{q}\sigma_{i}(A)^{mp},\quad\text{ for }q=1,\dotsc,d\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></munderover><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>q</mi></munderover><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for </mtext><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{q}\sigma_{i}(A^{m})^{p}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{q}\sigma_{i}(A)^{mp},\quad\text{ for }q=1,\dotsc,d\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for a matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the singular values of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Step <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows by using the above lemma for <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(I-\hat{\Lambda}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=d</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Corollary 3.5 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recalling the definition of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> given by (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Theorem 3.1 ‣ 3.1 In-Context Weight Prediction and Linear Self-attention ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=I-\left[(1+\frac{1}{n})\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I\right]^{-1}\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I-\left[(1+\frac{1}{n})\Lambda+\frac{1}{n}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I\right]^{-1}\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[(n+1)\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I]^{-1}(\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[(n+1)\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I]^{-1}(\Lambda+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq\frac{\lambda_{\min}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{(n+1)\lambda_{\min}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq\frac{\lambda_{\min}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}{(n+1)\lambda_{\min}+{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda)}I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}{n+1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖺𝗋𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖺𝗋𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}{n+1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+\frac{n}{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}\right)^{-1}I\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖺𝗋𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+\frac{n}{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}\right)^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2k})\leq d\left(1+\frac{n}{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}\right)^{-2k}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖺𝗋𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1}\Lambda)^{2k})\leq d\left(1+\frac{n}{1+{\sf{Hard}}(\Lambda)}\right)^{-2k}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof by invoking the result of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 ‣ 4 Task selection for training ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof follows a long the same lines as in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 ‣ 3.1 In-Context Weight Prediction and Linear Self-attention ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. Under the multi-task setting, each feature <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is now coming from a mixture of normal distributions. The main modification needed in the proof is on statement of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2 ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, which is extended as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with columns drawn i.i.d from a Gaussian mixture distribution, with probability <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf N}(0,\Lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf N}(0,\Lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any deterministic matrix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}A\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\right)=\frac{n-1}{n}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})A(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{\ell}(\Lambda_{\ell}(A+A^{\top})\Lambda_{\ell}+\Lambda_{\ell}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A\Lambda_{\ell}))\pi_{\ell}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\left(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}A\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\right)=\frac{n-1}{n}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})A(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{\ell}(\Lambda_{\ell}(A+A^{\top})\Lambda_{\ell}+\Lambda_{\ell}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A\Lambda_{\ell}))\pi_{\ell}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 ‣ A.6 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\Big(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\Big)=\frac{n-1}{n}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{\ell}(2\Lambda_{\ell}^{2}+\Lambda_{\ell}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda_{\ell}))\pi_{\ell}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\Big(\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\frac{XX^{\top}}{n}\Big)=\frac{n-1}{n}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{\ell}(2\Lambda_{\ell}^{2}+\Lambda_{\ell}{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Lambda_{\ell}))\pi_{\ell}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Continuing from (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}\left(\tilde{V}S\tilde{V}^{\top}\right)+\frac{d}{2}+c\;{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\tilde{V}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}{{\operatorname{tr}}}\left(\tilde{V}S\tilde{V}^{\top}\right)+\frac{d}{2}+c\;{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\tilde{V}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Setting the derivative to zero, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}(\tilde{V}(S+S^{\top}))+c\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L(\theta)=\frac{c^{2}}{2}(\tilde{V}(S+S^{\top}))+c\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Solving this equation, using that <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}=-\frac{1}{c}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})S^{-1}=\frac{1}{c}\Gamma^{-1}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}=-\frac{1}{c}(\sum_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell})S^{-1}=\frac{1}{c}\Gamma^{-1}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where the last step follows from the definition of <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 ‣ 4 Task selection for training ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is similar to the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.
Recall <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Sigma}:=\frac{1}{m}X_{{\rm test}}X_{{\rm test}}^{\top}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{k}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>test</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Sigma}:=\frac{1}{m}X_{{\rm test}}X_{{\rm test}}^{\top}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{k}x_{i}x_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, the empirical covariance of the features in the test prompt.
A major difference with the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, here we have to work with <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{-1}\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{-1}\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, neither of which are symmetric. To relate the trace of their powers to their singular values, we do a symmetrization step.
We write</p>
<table id="A1.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\dotsc(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\dotsc(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}\dotsc\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}\dotsc\Gamma^{-1/2}\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})\dotsc(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})\Gamma^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})\dotsc(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})\Gamma^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{1/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Gamma^{-1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex97.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{1/2}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{1/2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}\Gamma^{-1}(I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k}\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k}\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In the equalities above we used the identity <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\operatorname{tr}}}(AB)={{\operatorname{tr}}}(BA)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\operatorname{tr}}}(AB)={{\operatorname{tr}}}(BA)</annotation></semantics></math>. The inequalities follows from the fact that for positive semidefinite matrices <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\operatorname{tr}}}(AB)\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A){{\operatorname{tr}}}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\operatorname{tr}}}(AB)\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(A){{\operatorname{tr}}}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We next denote by <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the eigenvalues of <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\Sigma\Gamma^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\Sigma\Gamma^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.4 Hardness of a task ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we have <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k}\leq\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\tilde{\Delta}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k}\leq\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\tilde{\Delta}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})\leq Ck\sqrt{d/m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i})\leq Ck\sqrt{d/m}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By continuing from (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In A.7 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems and Technical Lemmas ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>), we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1})^{k}(I-\Gamma^{-1}\widehat{\Sigma})^{k})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[{{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\widehat{\Sigma}\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[\sum_{i=1}^{d}\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[\sum_{i=1}^{d}\hat{\sigma}_{i}^{2k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}(\tilde{\Delta}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+Ck\sqrt{d/m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma)\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sigma_{i}^{2k}(1+Ck\sqrt{d/m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma){{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\Sigma\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k})(1+o(1))\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma^{-1}){{\operatorname{tr}}}(\Gamma){{\operatorname{tr}}}((I-\Gamma^{-1/2}\Sigma\Gamma^{-1/2})^{2k})(1+o(1))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where in the last step we used that <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\sqrt{d/m}=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\sqrt{d/m}=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> by our assumption. This concludes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 4.3 ‣ 4.2 Optimal choice of task selection probabilities ‣ 4 Task selection for training ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof follows from the Markov inequality. Define a discrete random variable <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> which takes values <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X\leq 2(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))=\sum_{\ell\in[T]}\pi_{\ell}\mathbf{1}_{(\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})\leq 2(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))}=\sum_{\ell\in D}\pi_{\ell}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X\leq 2(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))=\sum_{\ell\in[T]}\pi_{\ell}\mathbf{1}_{(\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})\leq 2(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))}=\sum_{\ell\in D}\pi_{\ell}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In addition,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]=\sum\pi_{\ell}\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})\leq\sigma_{\min}(\sum\pi_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell})=\sigma_{\min}(\tilde{\Gamma})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]=\sum\pi_{\ell}\sigma_{\min}(\Lambda_{\ell})\leq\sigma_{\min}(\sum\pi_{\ell}\Lambda_{\ell})=\sigma_{\min}(\tilde{\Gamma}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">by using the convexity of minimum eigenvalue and Jensen’s inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recalling <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 4.1 ‣ 4 Task selection for training ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\succeq\frac{n-1}{n}\sum_{\ell\in[T]}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell}=\frac{n-1}{n}\tilde{\Gamma}\succeq\frac{1}{2}\tilde{\Gamma}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\succeq\frac{n-1}{n}\sum_{\ell\in[T]}\Lambda_{\ell}\pi_{\ell}=\frac{n-1}{n}\tilde{\Gamma}\succeq\frac{1}{2}\tilde{\Gamma}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A1.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the above two equations, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]\leq 2\sigma_{\min}(\Gamma)\leq 2(\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)+\varepsilon)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]\leq 2\sigma_{\min}(\Gamma)\leq 2(\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)+\varepsilon)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\ell\in D}\pi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\ell\in D}\pi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(X\leq 4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(X\leq 4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(X&gt;4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(X&gt;4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]}{4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}[X]}{4(\varepsilon+\sigma_{\min}(\Sigma))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where we used Markov’s inequality in the third step.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report additional experiments on a transformer with a single linear self-attention, when starting training from random initialization and performing CoT with length <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> during training.
Similar to the main paper, the data distribution follows our in-context weight prediction task in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 In-Context Weight Prediction and Linear Self-attention ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, where <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\tau,i}\sim{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\tau,i}\sim{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. We choose the token dimensions <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=10</annotation></semantics></math>. During inference, we let model to output <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> steps before outputting the final predicted weight vector. At each step <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> we concatenate the embedding with <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0_{d},\hat{w}_{i},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0_{d},\hat{w}_{i},1]</annotation></semantics></math> as in Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 In-Context Weight Prediction and Linear Self-attention ‣ 3 In-context Learning ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and input the concatenated embedding matrix to the model. The predicted <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> will be outputted after <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> steps of CoT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F4.sf1" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(a)</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F4.sf2" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(b)</span></a> show the test loss during training for <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2,4</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we train the model with <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20,40,80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20,40,80</annotation></semantics></math>. The training and test data are generated from <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\tau,i}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\tau,i}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\tau}\sim{\sf N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. We see that for a fixed value of <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, larger <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> yields a lower test error, which confirms our theoretical results.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F4.sf3" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Additional Experiments ‣ Understanding the Role of Training Data in Test-Time Scaling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(c)</span></a> shows the test loss during training when training distribution is skewed and some directions of the downstream task are not represented enough in the training data. from <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a skewed covariance matrix with eigenbasis chosen uniformly at random and <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th eigenvalue proportional to <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/i</annotation></semantics></math>.
For test, we sample prompt inputs from <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20</annotation></semantics></math>. We see that larger <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> yields a higher test error. Thus, larger test-time compute hurts the performance when some directions of the downstream data are not enough presented during training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03605v1/d=10_k=2_lr=0001_wd=00001_1.svg" id="A2.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A2.F4.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03605v1/d=10_k=4_lr=0001_wd=00001_1.svg" id="A2.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A2.F4.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=4</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A2.F4.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03605v1/d=5_n=10_lr=0001_wd=00001_skewed_2.svg" id="A2.F4.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/360;" width="476" height="360"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="A2.F4.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Skewed</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Transformer with a single linear self-attention. (a), (b) Fixing the test error, by increasing <math id="A2.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we can decrease the length of prompts <math id="A2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> during training. (c) When some directions of test are not enough represented in training data, more test-time compute hurst the performance.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
